rg 0311 ran 12:19Z to 12:23Z (4 min), with the PR #399 merge about 5 min after the ticket commit. Cite the source or write \"within minutes\". 0311's author is the author, relaying JETP-observer, and no source names padme as a reporter. The summary's \"G2's workaround\" rests on this unsourced claim.\n3. factcheck \u00b7 consider \u00b7 :58 (G1). 32 min runs from ticket creation to close (12:44Z to 13:16Z). PR #405 merged at 13:19:47Z, about 35 min after creation. Only the hook-reinstall note backs \"a clone sweep followed\".\n4. self + factcheck \u00b7 consider \u00b7 :56 (H1). \"Both were rewritten\" holds for cfh 3019 (log 2026-11-11T21:09Z, quote verbatim). 1522 kept its \"Web API with the read-write key\" choice and gained a superseding paragraph (lines 69-71). Both tickets carry the 2026-10-16 \"never the Web API\" phrase. The journal dates the local-only decision 2026-10-15 (tickets 1113/1111). \"The asker's framing\" is arguable, because 1522 cites \"author decisions of 2026-11-10\".\n5. self \u00b7 consider \u00b7 :57 (H2). The row is confirmed: relayed by a climate-finance-het session, 55 parents (42 added, 13 already there). The request originates with the author, and the ask offers one shape, so \"observation only\" is slightly strong.\nConfirmed without remark: P1 (padme 0086, 22 min from 20:12Z to 20:34Z, reported from an arena session, unread model card) and G1's ~40 KB, filer and reinstall note.\nSummary paragraph: its observation-versus-diagnosis contrast rests on H2 and P1, which hold, and on H1 (moderate) and P2 (does not hold as written). The return-path sentence holds for G1, but G2's half is unsourced.\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 3m22s\ntelemetry: wall=202s agents=1 tokens=~53k cost~=$0.3\nseat: factcheck \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=subagent \u00b7 model=anthropic/sonnet \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: self \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=self \u00b7 model=anthropi